# Royal Elementor Addons – Frontend CSS

`assets/css/frontend.css` is listed in **`.cursorignore`** so it stays out of Cursor indexing—treat it as if it does not exist.

**Do not open, edit, refactor, or search-replace `assets/css/frontend.css`.**

- The only editable frontend stylesheet is **`assets/css/frontend.min.css`**.
- Enqueued style path in PHP may say `frontend.css` or `frontend.min.css` per build; still edit **`frontend.min.css`** when the task is “change frontend CSS.”
- If something appears to require both files, **only change `frontend.min.css`**.
- Keep additions readable (non-minified) and scoped to REA selectors (e.g. `.wpr-*`).
- Do not minify CSS manually in chat edits. rea.local and rea-prod are separate. Never copy a file from one site onto the other unless the user explicitly names that site.
- To minify, run `npm run build:frontend-css` in the plugin folder you are working in. That rewrites only that folder's `frontend.min.css`. Do not use `rea-prod-frontend-minify` unless the user explicitly says rea-prod. Full steps are in `FRONTEND-MINIFYING.md`.
- Do not inject widget styles inline in PHP render methods.
